NOT TAX ADVICE
--------------
nz-fif is a calculation aid for New Zealand's foreign investment fund (FIF)
rules. It is not tax, legal or financial advice. It does not decide whether you
are a New Zealand tax resident, whether an interest is an attributing interest
in a FIF, whether an exemption (for example s EX 31 for ASX-listed Australian
companies) applies, whether you may use the fair dividend rate (FDR) or
comparative value (CV) method, or what you must file. Check every figure
against Inland Revenue guidance (IR461, IR3G) and a qualified New Zealand tax
adviser before using it in a return. The software is provided "AS IS", without
warranties or conditions of any kind (see sections 7 and 8 of the licence).

Third-party data bundled with this software
-------------------------------------------
- Reserve Bank of New Zealand, "Daily exchange rates and TWI - B1"
  (https://www.rbnz.govt.nz/statistics/series/exchange-and-interest-rates/exchange-rates-and-the-trade-weighted-index).
  Source: Reserve Bank of New Zealand, Reuters, NZFMA. "You are free to copy,
  distribute and adapt these statistics subject to the conditions listed on our
  copyright page." Snapshot details are in packages/core/data/README.md.

Third-party data fetched at run time (only when price lookup is on)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
- Yahoo Finance chart data, via the /api/price route. Unofficial endpoint;
  prices are shown to the user for review and can be overridden. Not affiliated
  with or endorsed by Yahoo.

